    "lawCode": "Amd §2802-a, Pub Health L; amd Part B §105, Chap 58 of 2005",
    "lawSection": "Public Health Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S3532\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to amend the public health law, in relation to the transitional\ncare unit demonstration program\n\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\n\nTo authorize the commissioner of health to approve the establishment\nand operation of additional transitional care units demonstrations in\ngeneral hospitals.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1 amends subdivision 1 of section 2802-a to the public health\nlaw to authorize an additional five transitional care unit\ndemonstration projects under the TCU demonstration program.\n\nSection 2 provides for an immediate effective date.\n\n EXISTING LAW :\nPHL 2802-a authorizes transitional care unit demonstration programs at\nup to five general hospitals.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nTransitional care units are designed to facilitate a smoother, more\ntimely and appropriate transition from acute care to discharge for\nthose patients 65 years or older. Discharge coming before a patient is\ntruly ready to be discharged may result in more frequent acute\nepisodes at higher cost. Last year the Legislature authorized up to\nfive demonstration programs. The interest in this program far exceeds\nthe limited number of demonstration sites authorized, expanding the\nnumber of authorized sites would allow a broader assessment of the\nimpact of TCD's.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n2007-2008: A.1313 - Remained in Committee 2005-2006: A.3722-A -\nRemained in committee 2003-2004: A.9343/S.5672 - Remained in Committee\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nTCUs would be eligible for Medicare reimbursement separate from\nMedicare's hospital prospective payment system.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately.\n",
